x86_64-windows  cxx1's listing carries three objects clang's does not: _CT??_R0D@81, _CTA1D and _TI1D - the catchable type, the array of those, and the ThrowInfo, for the `double` this case throws. cxx1 emits that chain for every throw of a type it can name; clang targeting the Microsoft ABI does not put them in this object. Measured, and one-directional: nothing clang emits here is missing from cxx1, and the type descriptor ??_R0N@8 itself agrees. x86_64-linux and arm64-darwin agree on every name. This case was a refusal until 2026-09-07 and carried no sidecar because names.sh skips a `.error` case; it is compared now that it runs.
